ed: LLR-335); test-cases.toml (re-attested: TC-360). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes."]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-902\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":702,"oldLines":3,"newStart":702,"newLines":9,"lines":[" date = \"2026-10-11\""," approved = [\"LLR-335\", \"TC-360\"]"," reattested = []","+","+[[act]]","+seq = 116","+date = \"2026-10-11\"","+approved = []","+reattested = [\"LLR-335\", \"TC-360\"]"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-902\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3450,"oldLines":8,"newStart":3450,"newLines":8,"lines":[" sr_refs = [\"SR-148\"]"," title = \"Adoption parsing and successor validation for an early disposition close\""," module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/adoption.py;project-trajectory/scripts/intake.py;project-trajectory/scripts/handback.py\"","-code_symbol = \"parse_block/disposed_id/row_refusal/_hits/parse_disposition_section/_section_block/adoption_lineage/_disposition_drafts/_merged_dispositions/_landed_before/_archive_one_adjudication_row\"","-detail = \"parse_block accepts only an adoption block holding one well-formed work-item id and otherwise returns the shape refusal. disposed_id reads the disposed item only from one event token in a disposition title and refuses a missing, ambiguous or non-disposition title. row_refusal reads the adopted item from the current registry and returns a distinct refusal when that registry cannot load, the item is not open at first consumption, its specification cannot read, or its Supersedes omits the disposed item; on a replay after the disposition was already consumed it finds the item in any state across the workspace and archive and reads lineage without re-reading open state. The close and the sweep that lands the disposition row consume an adoption with the open-state rule; a later sweep replays it with the lineage rule. Each accepted adoption joins its (adopted, disposed) lineage pair with drafted successors for one dependency re-point without minting another row; drafts remain drafts and still mint. Neither consumer guesses a successor or changes the adopted registry row's own cells.\"","+code_symbol = \"parse_block/disposed_id/work_specs/row_refusal/_hits/parse_disposition_section/_section_block/adoption_lineage/_disposition_drafts/_merged_dispositions/_landing_commit/_tree_specs/_tree_text/_archive_one_adjudication_row\"","+detail = \"parse_block accepts only an adoption block holding one well-formed work-item id and otherwise returns the shape refusal. disposed_id reads the disposed item only from one event token in a disposition title and refuses a missing, ambiguous or non-disposition title. row_refusal judges a listing of specifications and returns a distinct refusal when the listing cannot load, the item is not open, its specification cannot read, or its Supersedes omits the disposed item. The close judges trunk's working tree. Every sweep, including the landing sweep and a replay, judges the same open-state and Supersedes rule in the tree of the commit that landed the disposition row on trunk's first-parent line, so an adoption refused at landing stays refused and one accepted there stays accepted after its successor closes. A landing commit git cannot name, including one hidden by a shallow-clone boundary, refuses the sweep. The adopted specification is read from that tree as strict UTF-8; text that is not valid UTF-8 is unreadable and refuses with the distinct cannot-read reason. Each accepted adoption joins its (adopted, disposed) lineage pair with drafted successors for one dependency re-point without minting another row; drafts remain drafts and still mint. Neither consumer guesses a successor or changes the adopted item's identity, scope or Supersedes; the shared dependency re-point may rewrite its own needs edge to the disposed item.\""," rationale = \"An already-filed successor must be checked by the same rule wherever an early close is consumed; separate parsers would let one consumer close or mint from a successor the other rejects.\""," test_refs = \"TC-360\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-902\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3543,"oldLines":10,"newStart":3543,"newLines":10,"lines":[" [test.TC-360]"," verifies = [\"SR-148\", \"LLR-335\"]"," level = \"Integration\"","-method = \"Parse an adoption beside a draft and malformed adoption blocks; derive the disposed item from both valid title forms and reject absent, ambiguous or non-disposition titles; then read accepted, missing, closed, unreadable and non-superseding adopted rows from a temporary registry. On real repositories, confirm that a valid adoption closes and the landing sweep accepts it without minting, invalid or untokened adoptions refuse the close, a drafted successor beside an adoption still mints, and an adoption never becomes a consolidation absorption. Confirm that replay accepts an archived or closed adopted successor only on its lineage, still refuses a missing or non-superseding successor, and that the landing sweep still refuses a closed successor. Confirm that adoption and drafted-successor lineage re-point a dependent to the full successor set, including a dependent filed after a first sweep, then leave a second replay with no commit.\"","+method = \"Parse an adoption beside a draft and malformed adoption blocks; derive the disposed item from both valid title forms and reject absent, ambiguous or non-disposition titles; then read accepted, missing, closed, unreadable and non-superseding adopted rows from a temporary registry. On real repositories, confirm that a valid adoption closes and the landing sweep accepts it without minting, invalid or untokened adoptions refuse the close, a drafted successor beside an adoption still mints, and an adoption never becomes a consolidation absorption. Confirm that every sweep judges the open-state and Supersedes rule in the landing commit's tree: a valid adoption stays accepted after its successor completes, while adoptions refused at landing because their successor was complete or cancelled refuse again without changing the dependent or trunk. Confirm that a disposition whose landing commit cannot be read, including one past a shallow boundary, refuses with nothing written, and that a successor specification not valid UTF-8 in the landing tree is unreadable at landing and on replay after only the current file is repaired. Confirm that adoption and drafted-successor lineage re-point a dependent to the full successor set, including a dependent filed after a first sweep, then leave a second replay with no commit.\""," tier = \"Full\"","-expected = \"Satisfies SR-148 through LLR-335: a well-formed adoption is accepted only while open at first consumption, then replays by its enduring lineage; invalid lineage refuses; and its dependency re-point preserves the complete successor set without allocating an id.\"","+expected = \"Satisfies SR-148 through LLR-335: a well-formed adoption is accepted by the close from trunk's working tree and by every sweep only when open and superseding in the landing commit's tree; unknown or unreadable historical input refuses with nothing written; and its dependency re-point preserves the complete successor set without allocating an id.\""," automated = \"Yes\"","-evidence = \"tests/test_disposition_adoption.py::test_an_adoption_block_is_parsed_apart_from_the_drafts; tests/test_disposition_adoption.py::test_a_malformed_adoption_block_is_a_parse_refusal; tests/test_disposition_adoption.py::test_the_disposed_row_is_read_from_either_minted_title_form; tests/test_disposition_adoption.py::test_acceptance_is_read_against_the_registry_with_distinct_refusals; tests/test_disposition_adoption.py::test_an_adoption_never_counts_as_an_absorption; tests/test_handback.py::test_an_a