{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvkvPrjuaDDhWE8kcMWw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both rows changed meaning, and I blessed and re-anchored both. That took two commits, each ending `WI: WI-902`, and the commit checks passed on both:\n\n| Commit | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `ad63f4519` | The verdict: `VERDICT: MEANING rows=2`, `SITTING: JUDGED kinds=amendment`. The sitting parser accepts it. |\n| `a588ae83f` | `snapshot --reattests LLR-335,TC-360`. No other drifted row blocked it. |\n\n**Why MEANING:**\n- **LLR-335:** the old text let a later sweep accept an adoption on lineage alone. The new text judges every sweep by the same open-and-superseding rule, in the tree of the commit that landed the disposition. It adds two refusals: a landing git can't name (including one hidden by a shallow-clone boundary), and an adopted spec that isn't valid UTF-8. It also narrows the \"changes no cells\" clause so the shared re-point may rewrite the adopted item's own needs edge. Code that met the old text, the lineage-only replay ruling 009 struck down, fails the new text.\n- **TC-360:** the old Method required lineage-only acceptance; the new one forbids it and adds checks for the landing tree, the shallow boundary and UTF-8.\n\n**Why I blessed them:**\n- **Parent:** judging \"open and superseding\" at the landing commit is what SR-148's \"already-open item that supersedes it\" means, evaluated where the choice was made.\n- **Single home:** LLR-335 is still the one home for adoption, and LLR-153 still cites it rather than restating it.\n- **Code match:** the text matches the code. `_landing_commit` returns nothing at a shallow boundary (`intake.py:1856`), and `_tree_text` decodes strict UTF-8 (`intake.py:1891`).\n- **Trace cells:** all 14 code symbols named by LLR-335 exist, and nothing still references the removed `_landed_before` or the deleted test.\n- **Tests:** all 18 tests cited by TC-360 exist, and the four new ones assert what the Method claims:\n  - refused-then-replayed, for complete and cancelled successors;\n  - a landing git can't name, and a landing past a shallow boundary on a real shallow clone;\n  - a non-UTF-8 spec, refused at landing and again after only the current file is repaired.\n\nThe narrowed clause also settles review 008's minor finding and my advisory 2 from sitting 007. Advisory 1 from that sitting still stands: the shared intake functions tag only LLR-335, not LLR-153. It wasn't part of this question.\n\nThe untracked `013-ADJUDICATE-6bf8953.md.requested` is the coordinator's, and I didn't touch it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1091,"cache_read_input_tokens":302589,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1091},"output_tokens":765,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73ae5cf9-d335-4bb7-a08f-7631da597f26","uuid":"0f443294-a90c-4585-933d-3c4209150b10","timestamp":"2026-10-11T16:23:02.952Z","request_id":"req_011CfvkvParqvjW6coN1JJ7K"}
